{
  "id": 21,
  "name": "density_scaled_regret",
  "intent": "Amplify the regret term relative to the parent by scaling it with cluster density, since regret (second-nearest minus nearest among unvisited) is most informative when nearest-other distances are small and reliable (dense regions). Keep local distance dominant, retain a mild late-game return boost for closure, and add a small spread penalty to avoid candidates that are unevenly connected to the remaining set. Distance still dominates; regret becomes a stronger tie-breaker, especially in clustered instances where pure nearest-neighbor can prematurely anchor the tour on a boundary node.",
  "tags": [
    "regret",
    "cluster"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    r = f['return_distance']\n    g = f['regret']\n    p = f['progress']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    sp = f['spread']\n    return -d + 0.25 * r + 0.15 * p * r + (0.35 + 0.25 * cd) * g - 0.05 * sp",
  "source": "live_llm",
  "parent_id": 20,
